{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider did coordinate and the driver did not answer. EV-CHAT-02703 shows the driver writing 'hi im at the bay, where are you' at 07:53:25 and the rider replying 'coming' at 07:55:20, inside the waiting window; the driver posted nothing in the following 120 seconds and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, so limbs (a) and (b) of POL-NS-04 are made out. Limb (c) is not, and I do not pretend otherwise: the rider's own track in EV-GPS-02703 places the rider's device between 796.46 m and 804.18 m from the pickup pin (mean 800.51 m) across all 90 fixes, with rider_qualifying_fix_count 0 against the 200 m rider-presence radius for TRANSPORT_HUB. Even on the reading most favourable to the rider - limb (c) undecidable because no fix survives the accuracy filter, POL-NS-11 - the clause still cannot exonerate, so this route yields the rider no refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02703", "EV-GPS-02703", "EV-TRIP-02703"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The waiting-period arithmetic runs against the rider and I state it rather than stretch it. The free waiting period in force is 300 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, carried on EV-TRIP-02703), and the derived arrival facts in EV-GPS-02703 show one continuous in-geofence run of 556 seconds, from 07:53:00 to 08:02:16, that is a shortfall of -256 seconds. The cancellation at 08:02:20 is 556 seconds after the first qualifying in-geofence fix, so it also falls at or after the 480 second no_show_threshold_sec in force. POL-NS-06 - the rider's cleanest arithmetic route to a full refund of the cancellation-fee line - cannot be run on these numbers, and POL-NS-01 limb (c) is satisfied on them. EV-FARE-02703 shows the $5.00 cancellation fee charged with refund_issued_sgd 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02703", "EV-TRIP-02703", "EV-FARE-02703"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's side does not concede platform-confirmed arrival. The event chain in EV-TRIP-02703 runs driver_assigned, driver_en_route, driver_arrived, wait_timer_started, trip_cancelled - there is no wait_timer_expired event. POL-NS-12 makes the platform's GPS_AUTO arrival and wait-timer events a carrier independent of the exported trace only where wait_timer_started AND wait_timer_expired are both carried, so on this record that route is not made out and the arrival and served-dwell facts must come out of the exported trace. I disclose honestly that this does not by itself displace the fee: EV-GPS-02703 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and shows the same 556 second continuous run, so the gap in the event chain removes a carrier without removing the fact the driver needs.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02703", "EV-GPS-02703"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No advisory covers the pickup road: EV-ADVIS-02703-01 is MISSING, carries issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, and has no payload. Under POL-NS-06 limb (i) a present and populated traffic_advisory is the only thing that permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed, and under POL-GEN-02 a MISSING artifact can carry no fact at all. The rider therefore puts the driver's side to proof of any advisory-based excuse for its position or its intervals; the record supplies none. This is a citable absence rather than a fact, and it produces no refund here, because the driver's dwell is a single uninterrupted 556 second run that needs no accumulation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02703-01", "EV-GPS-02703"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}
